Package: RegCompassR
Title: Multiome Regulatory Evidence and Metabolic Reaction Analysis
Version: 1.8.4
Authors@R: c(person(given = "RegCompass", family = "Developers", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "dev@example.com"))
Author: RegCompass Developers [aut, cre]
Maintainer: RegCompass Developers <dev@example.com>
Description: Fits condition-by-cell-type Pando models for Human-GEM or
    Mouse-GEM GPR target genes in paired single-cell RNA and ATAC data,
    identifies metabolic target genes with significant TF-peak-gene evidence,
    maps complete-GPR core reactions, and expands annotation-defined biological
    meta-modules. Meta-modules are deduplicated into a merged reaction catalogue
    without local FASTCORE completion. For each medium scenario, the package
    constructs one shared union GEM and performs a single global FASTCORE
    completion before directional COMPASS-like scoring. Integrated RNA and ATAC
    evidence is converted to reaction penalties. A post-Layer-2 step can score
    non-core reactions directly sharing KEGG, Reactome, or master-Rhea
    identifiers with selected cores in the exact cached medium-specific union
    GEM used for the original analysis. Pinned human and mouse GEMs are bundled
    for offline use, with platform-aware parallel execution and audited progress
    and timing output.
